    <string name="light_source_dot">Light source %1$s</string>
    <string name="measure_hint">Place the phone flat under the lamp, screen facing up · Swipe to change the light source</string>
    <string name="measure_no_sensor">This device has no light sensor.</string>
    <string name="warn_sensor_saturated">Sensor saturated – reading unreliable</string>
    <string name="label_explanation">How the measurement works</string>
    <string name="measure_guide">Place the phone flat under the lamp at canopy height, screen facing up. Do not cover the light sensor (usually at the top next to the front camera).</string>
    <string name="ppfd_explanation_1">Lux describes how bright light appears to the human eye. PPFD states how many photons usable for photosynthesis (PAR, 400–700 nm) hit one square meter per second – the light plants actually work with.</string>
    <string name="ppfd_explanation_2">The conversion factor depends on the light source: the eye weights green strongly but red and blue hardly at all. Every lamp has a different spectrum, so the same number of lux contains a different amount of PAR.</string>
    <string name="ppfd_explanation_3">The values are only rough guide values. Phone light sensors barely register red and blue light, are imprecise and sit behind the display glass. Use a PAR meter for accurate values.</string>
    <string name="ppfd_formula">PPFD = lux × factor (sun 0.018 · LED 0.014 · HPS 0.014 · fluorescent 0.013)</string>
    <string name="btn_ok">OK</string>

